<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, alcohol, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. He misses the whispered voice on the left. The lipid panel at the first visit showed total cholesterol 184, HDL 52, and LDL 112 mg/dL. [S]<list><item>Audiology for hearing testing.</item><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Prostate cancer, unfavorable intermediate risk, on androgen deprivation before radiotherapy (C61)</content>. Planned treatment on track: radiotherapy begins in about six weeks, after fiducial markers are placed. [S]<list><item>Follow-up in five weeks with PSA, testosterone, and vitamin D, and the second leuprolide injection.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Androgen deprivation therapy (Z79.899)</content>. Mild hot flashes and slightly lower afternoon energy, both expected; no treatment wanted. Blood pressure 132/76 mm Hg. Mood and cognition normal. [S]<list><item>Keep walking and add light resistance exercise, which helps fatigue, muscle, and bone on androgen deprivation.</item><item>Layered clothing and a cool bedroom for hot flashes; medicines such as venlafaxine are available if they become troublesome.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; no earlier pneumococcal vaccine on record; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>High-dose vaccine when this season&apos;s supply arrives in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>A single dose is recommended at 75 and older; at the pharmacy before the winter</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age with this season&apos;s vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven years ago; next dose due in three years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Screening from 76 to 85 is selective; discussed, and not recommended for him now, given his age and his current cancer treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA eight weeks ago before androgen deprivation: femoral neck T-score -1.4, spine -0.6; repeat in one to two years</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 184, HDL 52, LDL 112 mg/dL at the first visit; no diabetes or smoking. Risk calculators are not validated beyond 79, and evidence for starting a statin for primary prevention after 75 is limited; androgen deprivation adds some cardiometabolic risk. Not started after discussion; lipids and glucose again in one year on the androgen deprivation schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Outside the recommended age ranges and no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 10 seconds; no falls; walking and resistance exercise continue</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Referred</td><td>Whispered-voice test missed on the left; audiology arranged</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Five months ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, prostate cancer monograph (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Chronic-care follow-up in five weeks with the second leuprolide injection. Radiotherapy to start in about six weeks. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Audiology. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2001-07-14: three-month follow-up on androgen deprivation before radiotherapy: PSA, testosterone, vitamin D, and side effects. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent. He named a health care agent, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He said that what matters most to him is being told the truth about his health, continuing his work for as long as he can, and making his own decisions. He chose not to record specific treatment preferences today. The plan will be revisited yearly and with any change in his health. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
